 ["PR 101 formal RecursiveEngine routing oracle before typed dependency edges"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "The existing abstract PathDependencies function resolves an arrow-permission target by permission name alone because its compiled path has no resolved target resource type. Reusing that abstraction as an exact production SCC-routing oracle can connect an unrelated same-named permission to a recursive component."
 :fix
 "The executable production-routing oracle now consumes fully typed PermissionDependencyEdge values whose head and target are complete PermissionNode identities. The older path abstraction remains explicitly documented as a conservative cache-scope abstraction rather than an exact routing refinement."
